  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1253 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nHigh pressure will move in for mid-week and temperatures will \nreally start to feel cooler on Tuesday and Wednesday. Though, \nthis will be more near average for this time of year. Dewpoints \nwill finally dip into the 50s Tuesday night making the evenings/mornings\nfeel nice and cool as temperatures sit in the 50s. Daytime \nhighs will be in the 70s and 80s to end the week with more rain \nreturning this weekend as the next front moves through. Rain\nbecomes more widespread Friday into Saturday with 20-40% POPs as\nthe ridge begins to breakdown. Rain continues in the morning, \ndecreasing through the day (15-20%), then back up to 20-40% \nSaturday into Sunday as the front slowly moves through. Highs\nthis weekend will be in the 80s again.",
